WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.820
A dim corridor.

2
00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:04.650
At the very end of it, a plain door.

3
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.520
Caption one: "The door opened."

4
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.480
It swings smoothly.

5
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.980
Nothing else happens.

6
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:15.870
Caption two, over the same still
frame: "the door gave way."

7
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:16.900
Same door.

8
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.420
Same corridor.

9
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.590
So why does the second
caption make you lean in?

10
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.420
In this mission, you'll
test the easy answers.

11
00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.470
Is the second caption just longer?

12
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.170
Does it sound more formal?

13
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.530
Then you'll put one plain
verb under the microscope.

14
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.380
Walked.

15
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.280
Trudged.

16
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.300
Strode.

17
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.310
Crept.

18
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.780
And you'll explore connotations,
in words like slender,

19
00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.710
skinny and scrawny.

20
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: explain why the
second caption tells a story.
